hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27615","Haddathana Abu Asim, he said: Haddathana Thawr, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from Abd Allah ibn Busr, from his sister, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not fast Saturday except what has been obligated upon you, and if one of you finds nothing except a grapevine stick or the bark of a tree, let him chew it."
"27616","Haddathana Yahya ibn Ishaq, he said: Akhbarana Ibn Lahi'ah, he said: Akhbarana Musa ibn Wardan, from Ubayd al-A'raj, he said: My grandmother narrated to me that she entered upon the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was eating lunch, and that was Saturday, so he said: Come and eat. She said: I am fasting. So he said to her: Did you fast yesterday? She said: No. He said: Then eat, for fasting Saturday is neither for you nor against you."
"27617","Haddathana al-Hakam ibn Nafi', he said: Haddathana Isma'il ibn Ayyash, from Muhammad ibn al-Walid al-Zubaydi, from Luqman ibn Amir, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from Abd Allah ibn Busr, from his sister al-Samma', from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Let none of you fast Saturday except in an obligation, and if he finds nothing except the bark of a tree, let him break his fast with it."
